      },
      {
        "text": "Then the priest shall go out of the house to the door of the house, and shut up the house seven days:",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 38,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Leviticus 14:38",
        "book": "Leviticus",
        "chapter": 14,
        "verse": 38
      },
      {
        "text": "And the priest shall come again the seventh day, and shall look: and, behold, if the plague be spread in the walls of the house;",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 78,
            "end": 80
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 39,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Leviticus 14:39",
        "book": "Leviticus",
        "chapter": 14,
        "verse": 39
      },
      {
        "text": "Then the priest shall command that they take away the stones in which the plague is, and they shall cast them into an unclean place without the city:",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 81,
            "end": 84
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 40,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Leviticus 14:40",
        "book": "Leviticus",
        "chapter": 14,
        "verse": 40
      },
      {
        "text": "And he shall cause the house to be scraped within round about, and they shall pour out the dust that they scrape off without the city into an unclean place:",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 41,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Leviticus 14:41",
        "book": "Leviticus",
        "chapter": 14,
        "verse": 41
      },
      {
        "text": "And they shall take other stones, and put them in the place of those stones; and he shall take other mortar, and shall plaster the house.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 42,
            "end": 46
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 42,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Leviticus 14:42",
        "book": "Leviticus",
        "chapter": 14,
        "verse": 42
      },
      {
        "text": "And if the plague come again, and break out in the house, after that he hath taken away the stones, and after he hath scraped the house, and after it is plastered;",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 77,
            "end": 87,
            "text": "HEB extracted."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 43,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Leviticus 14:43",
        "book": "Leviticus",
        "chapter": 14,
        "verse": 43
      },
      {
        "text": "Then the priest shall come and look, and, behold, if the plague be spread in the house, it is a fretting leprosy in the house: it is unclean.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 96,
            "end": 104,
            "text": "HEB malignant."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 50,
            "end": 52
          },
          {
            "start": 91,
            "end": 93
          },
          {
            "start": 130,
            "end": 132
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 44,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Leviticus 14:44",
        "book": "Leviticus",
        "chapter": 14,
        "verse": 44
      },
      {
        "text": "And he shall break down the house, the stones of it, and the timber thereof, and all the mortar of the house; and he shall carry them forth out of the city into an unclean place.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 129,
            "end": 133
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 45,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Leviticus 14:45",
        "book": "Leviticus",
        "chapter": 14,
        "verse": 45
      },
      {
        "text": "Moreover he that goeth into the house all the while that it is shut up shall be unclean until the even.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 46,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Leviticus 14:46",
        "book": "Leviticus",
        "chapter": 14,
        "verse": 46
      },
      {
        "text": "And he that lieth in the house shall wash his clothes; and he that eateth in the house shall wash his clothes.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 47,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Leviticus 14:47",
        "book": "Leviticus",
        "chapter": 14,
        "verse": 47
      },
      {
        "text": "And if the priest shall come in, and look upon it, and, behold, the plague hath not spread in the house, after the house was plastered: then the priest shall pronounce the house clean, because the plague is healed.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 42,
            "end": 50
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 48,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Leviticus 14:48",
        "book": "Leviticus",
        "chapter": 14,
        "verse": 48
      },
      {
        "text": "And he shall take to cleanse the house two birds, and cedar wood, and scarlet, and hyssop:",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 21,
            "end": 28,
            "text": "TG Purification."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 49,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "TG Purification.",
            "prettyString": "TG Purification",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "studyHelp",
                "studyHelpType": "tg",
                "title": "Purification",
                "entryId": "tg-purification",
                "book": "",
                "chapters": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Leviticus 14:49",
        "book": "Leviticus",
        "chapter": 14,
        "verse": 49
      },
      {
        "text": "And he shall kill the one of the birds in an earthen vessel over running water:",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 50,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Leviticus 14:50",
        "book": "Leviticus",
        "chapter": 14,
        "verse": 50
      },
      {
        "text": "And he shall take the cedar wood, and the hyssop, and the scarlet, and the living bird, and dip them in the blood of the slain bird, and in the running water, and sprinkle the house seven times:",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 51,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Leviticus 14:51",
        "book": "Leviticus",
        "chapter": 14,
        "verse": 51
      },
      {
        "text": "And he shall cleanse the house with the blood of the bird, and with the running water, and with the living bird, and with the cedar wood, and with the hyssop, and with the scarlet:",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 52,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Leviticus 14:52",
        "book": "Leviticus",
        "chapter": 14,
        "verse": 52
      },
      {
        "text": "But he shall let go the living bird out of the city into the open fields, and make an atonement for the house: and it shall be clean.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 53,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Leviticus 14:53",
        "book": "Leviticus",
        "chapter": 14,
        "verse": 53
      },
      {
        "text": "This is the law for all manner of plague of leprosy, and scall,",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 57,
            "end": 62,
            "text": "HEB tinea or other scaly symptoms."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 5,
            "end": 7
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 54,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Leviticus 14:54",
        "book": "Leviticus",
        "chapter": 14,
        "verse": 54
      },
      {
        "text": "And for the leprosy of a garment, and of a house,",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 12,
            "end": 19,
            "text": "Lev. 13:59 (47–59)."
          },
          {
            "start": 43,
            "end": 48,
            "text": "Lev. 14:34 (33–53)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 55,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Leviticus 14:55",
        "book": "Leviticus",
        "chapter": 14,
        "verse": 55
      },
      {
        "text": "And for a rising, and for a scab, and for a bright spot:",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 56,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Leviticus 14:56",
        "book": "Leviticus",
        "chapter": 14,
        "verse": 56
      },
      {
        "text": "To teach when it is unclean, and when it is clean: this is the law of leprosy.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 14,
